    {
      "ts": "2026-02-11T22:22:15.935-08:00",
      "player": "Gem3F Vorthos",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "A flashy Slickshot Show-Off attempts to steal the stage with its aerobatics! A 1/2 flyer with the potential to grow based on noncreature spells cast by the Analyst. My noble Momo, the Friendly Flier, or even the draconic Sarkhan himself could stand in its way. \n\
\n\
However, Sarkhan's destiny lies in becoming a Dragon, and Momo is but a small companion. Blocking with either could be risky if the Analyst has spells to bolster their performer. \n\
\n\
Let's see. If I block with Sarkhan (2/2), he trades if they have nothing, or survives if they don't pump it. If I block with Momo (1/1), Momo likely dies. \n\
\n\
Taking 1 (or more) damage isn't the end of the world for a Vorthos who plays the long game. The Show-Off is a mere distraction compared to the dragons we shall summon. I'll decline to block and let the \"Show-Off\" have its moment in the sun.\n\
\n\
I choose not to block.\n\
