      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem25F Analyst skipped their land drop on turn 2 with two lands in hand (Mountain and Rockface Village). Missing a land drop is significant, especially when they have a hand full of spells that need mana - three Slickshot Show-Offs (each costing 1R), Lightning Helix (RW), and Nova Hellkite (3RR). Playing Mountain here would allow them to have 2 mana on turn 2, enabling a Slickshot Show-Off or Lightning Helix to kill Momo. Even if they wanted to hold up mana or sequence differently, there is no reason to skip a land drop entirely when you have lands in hand and expensive cards to cast.",
      "action_taken": "Skipped land drop entirely on turn 2, leaving only 1 land (Sunbillow Verge) in play.",
      "better_line": "Play Mountain (or Rockface Village) to have 2 mana available. Could then cast Slickshot Show-Off or use Lightning Helix to remove Momo, Friendly Flier before it generates value. At minimum, developing mana is essential to cast the cards in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 13,
      "player": "Gem25F Analyst",
      "decision_index": 8,
