    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Slickshot Show-Off in the precombat main phase rather than plotting it or waiting. With 3 lands and Slickshot having haste, casting it precombat is fine for attacking this turn. However, the opponent has Momo (1/1 flying) and Sarkhan (2/2) on board. The key question is whether casting Slickshot now versus plotting one (to deploy it for free next turn alongside noncreature spells) would be better. Casting precombat with a creature that has haste is generally correct since you want to attack. But with 3 Slickshot Show-Offs in hand, plotting one this turn (spending the same 1R) to set up a bigger burst turn next turn with multiple Slickshots + burn spells could be more explosive. That said, applying pressure now with the 1/2 flyer is reasonable, and plotting doesn't generate immediate board presence. The more notable consideration is whether to use Burst Lightning or Lightning Helix on Sarkhan first before combat, since Sarkhan could become a Dragon threat if the opponent plays Nova Hellkite or another Dragon. But overall, casting Slickshot precombat with haste to attack is defensible.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Slickshot Show-Off in precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Consider plotting a Slickshot Show-Off instead (same mana cost) to set up a more explosive future turn where you can deploy it for free alongside burn spells to trigger its +2/+0 ability multiple times. Alternatively, cast Burst Lightning targeting Sarkhan before it can grow, then cast Slickshot.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 25,
